# Sociology as a Discipline: Quasi-Science and Quasi- Humanities.

**Authors:** Zald, Mayer N.

## Abstract
Traces the occupational and intellectual components of sociology's effort to win recognition as a science. Focuses on the model of science used and its limits. Argues that sociology, as quasi-science and quasi-humanities, should be maintaining the empirical outlook of a science while recognizing the impact of civilization on concepts and theories. (DK)

